  "style": {
    "name": "Polychrome Helian (Painted Sun-Temple)",
    "rationale": "Reworked the first pass into a coherent painted-marble order: white fluted quartz columns in a clean hexastyle rhythm with a wide central portal, set against a deep-blue cella so the colonnade reads with real porch shadow. The messy floating crown is replaced by a true shallow pediment (1:3 rake, smoothed with stairs) holding a golden sun in a blue tympanum, with gold acroteria. Polychrome triglyph-and-metope frieze (cyan/orange/red/gold) keeps the bold color the original had, but balanced and symmetric. Crepidoma stepped and trimmed with cyan and gold bands; door given a stepped arch and gold frame for relief depth."
  },
